I prepared a standalone, fully compiled LaTeX note. It uses the uploaded article’s pure-chordal theorem and clique-tree entropy construction as its starting point. fileciteturn6file0L149-L171 fileciteturn6file0L209-L256 The monotone-\((b_j)\) extension and the pooled bound for arbitrary chordal graphs are derived additions, not claims extracted from the source; the note explicitly makes no literature-priority claim.

The source includes:

- the chromatic-polynomial factorization for arbitrary connected chordal graphs;
- the intrinsic interpretation of
  \[
  b_j=\#\{i:r_i\ge j\}-\#\{e:s_e\ge j\};
  \]
- the common uniform-\(K_r\) marginal construction;
- a complete junction-tree entropy lemma;
- the entropy-deficit suffix inequalities obtained from Moon–Moser;
- the Abel-summation proof under \(b_1\le\cdots\le b_r\);
- the equivalent structural condition \(m_j\le a_j\);
- the graphon approximation and both boundary cases;
- the pool-adjacent-violators argument and the resulting explicit bound for every connected chordal graph;
- detailed non-pure examples, including a triangle with pendant leaves.

The source compiles without warnings; I also rendered and checked the resulting 16-page PDF.

